# Line-ending rules.
#
# The laptop is Windows and the Pi is Linux, so git normally converts to
# CRLF on checkout. That is fine for text, and BREAKS executables: a shell
# script with CRLF fails on Linux with the famously unhelpful
#     bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M
# and a systemd unit with CRLF is silently mis-parsed.
#
# Force LF for anything Linux executes directly.

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf

# Pixelblaze patterns get pasted into a web editor; keep them stable too.
*.js        text eol=lf

# Audio and images must never be touched.
*.wav       binary
*.ogg       binary
*.mp3       binary
*.flac      binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.mp4       binary

# Fonts are binary; never let line-ending conversion near them.
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary
